1176
01:03:39,747 --> 01:03:47,854
[SPEAKER_03]: I pitched on the sand lots, and I could beat anybody in the world on them when I was over there in the Jersey prison.

1177
01:03:47,894 --> 01:03:49,095
[SPEAKER_03]: These good clubs.

1178
01:03:50,116 --> 01:03:56,221
[SPEAKER_03]: And I, in 1921, from 20 on, I had all kinds of offers to play.

1179
01:03:57,041 --> 01:04:04,408
[SPEAKER_03]: I wasn't in any hurry because I had a job over in New York, the county clerk's office, a civil service job.

1180
01:04:04,968 --> 01:04:05,929
[SPEAKER_03]: I could go out and make

1181
01:04:06,663 --> 01:04:10,666
[SPEAKER_02]: money pitching during the week.

1182
01:04:10,826 --> 01:04:19,493
[SPEAKER_03]: And I could pitch a game during the week and make, well, $50, sometimes $75, which was good money in those days.

1183
01:04:20,073 --> 01:04:21,254
[SPEAKER_03]: So I was in no hurry.

1184
01:04:21,815 --> 01:04:25,017
