1194
01:04:49,418 --> 01:04:51,058
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay, how ready are you?

1195
01:04:51,078 --> 01:04:52,199
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, I'll share one with him.

1196
01:04:52,219 --> 01:04:53,460
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, then I'll have a Coke for you.

1197
01:04:54,180 --> 01:04:58,722
[SPEAKER_03]: And, you see, I pitched till I was 28 years old on the sand lines.

1198
01:04:59,703 --> 01:05:02,724
[SPEAKER_03]: And that was a lot of pitching in those years, after all.

1199
01:05:03,024 --> 01:05:03,925
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't realize you were

1200
01:05:04,598 --> 01:05:06,879
[SPEAKER_01]: So older when you went up.

1201
01:05:06,899 --> 01:05:12,602
[SPEAKER_03]: If they knew that I was 38 or 39, they would have gotten rid of me before that.

1202
01:05:13,203 --> 01:05:15,704
[SPEAKER_03]: They thought I was about four or five years younger.

1203
01:05:16,945 --> 01:05:25,029
[SPEAKER_03]: But I had pitched a lot of my baseball before I ever got anything, which was all right with me because I did well.

1204
